  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "a base written as a subscript -- class Ids(RootModel[list[int]]) -- emits no relation.implements in omega-python, so a parameterized RootModel is not recognized as a model",
      "a keyword argument is not readable: omega-python's call.arg0_text strips one leading and one trailing quote byte, so Field(alias=\"userId\") arrives as alias=\"userId and ConfigDict(frozen=True) as frozen=True. Aliases, field constraints, model_validator(mode=...) and every ConfigDict setting are therefore not stated, although the positional field name of a validator or serializer now is",
      "only the first field name of a multi-field @field_validator(\"a\", \"b\") is stated; call.arg1_text carries the second but is indistinguishable from a keyword argument, which would render an edge to a field that does not exist",
      "a decorator written as an attribute -- @pydantic.field_validator(\"x\") -- emits call.method rather than call.function, so its validated field is not stated",
      "a decorator's span neither contains nor is contained by the span of the function it decorates, so which method implements a validator or serializer is not statable",
      "dynamic validators/serializers created by metaprogramming, model_rebuild effects and runtime validation are runtime semantics",
      "generated JSON Schema is not executed; authored model classes, fields, Field declarations, validators/serializers, ConfigDict declarations and model parse/dump call sites are materialized",
      "forward-reference target resolution and complex Annotated metadata require generic type/value resolution, not Framework guessing"
    ]
  },
